      "side": 1,
      "message": "Role and compression mode probably not? I think the primary usage for redaction is to ensure that privileged or location-sensitive information is not passed to apps in callbacks.\n\nSome of this information might potentially be placed into a TransportInfo instead of a NetworkSpecifier, but note that the TransportInfo is only sent to callbacks and does not participate in request matching. So if apps need to be able to file requests for a given remote MAC address, then it needs to be in the specifier.\n\nRemember also that redaction only removes the information when calling a callback, but that information still participates in request matching. So if an app is able to file a request for a given MAC address, that request will still get onAvailable if a network with that MAC address connects, and so the app will implicitly know that a network with that MAC address exists.",
      "parentUuid": "bde305c3_234be0f4",
